 "notes": "3-sigma exclusion from Bayesian analysis of GW170817 inspiral (Fig. 1, blue 'GW170817' region; vector paths extracted from constraints.pdf in the e-print, axes calibrated with tick-label positions). The excluded region is a BAND in the (m_a, 1/f_a) plane: 1e-18 GeV^-1 < 1/f_a < ~6.4e-17 GeV^-1 (i.e. 1.6e16 GeV < f_a < 1e18 GeV) for m_a below ~1e-11 eV; axions with f_a > 1e18 GeV are not sourced by neutron stars (no in-medium phase transition), so the band's lower boundary at 1/f_a = 1e-18 GeV^-1 is a theoretical applicability cutoff. The data_points trace the upper (data-driven) boundary of the excluded band, i.e. the measured constraint f_a < 1.6e16 GeV (flat part) including the per-sampled-mass wiggles at m_a ~ 1e-13 to 2e-11 eV; the constraint is extrapolated to the massless limit (figure starts at m_a = 1e-21 eV). Confidence level is 3 sigma (~99.7%), as stated in the abstract. No dark-matter density assumption (constraint from axion force/radiation in the binary inspiral).",
